## Part 5: Summary of changes and why (quick reference)

| # | Change | Primary reason |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Split client store into Canon Cache / Episode Workspace / Job Mirror | Different lifecycles; server owns jobs |
| 2 | Canon versioning + WKW as append-only ledger + reviewable carry-forward | Continuity becomes auditable and reversible |
| 3 | Character Registry as a service; detect at script time; alias resolution | Onboarding is a canon event, not an image side effect |
| 4 | Continuity Pack + Prompt Assembler + per-frame provenance | Deterministic look; reproducible frames |
| 5 | Aspect → Output Profile on assets, not a global toggle | Prevents cross-format asset mismatch; enables dual-format |
| 6 | **Render Manifest** as the browser↔kit contract | Two renderers, one input; true portability |
| 7 | Domain Services vs. Provider Adapters | Swappability, testability, one place for cost telemetry |
| 8 | Move Motion .txt to Export; replace "GitHub Hygiene" with Secret Scrub Gate | Right responsibility, enforceable guarantee |
| 9 | Provider-aware `voiceProfile` + Voice Map | ElevenLabs/Gemini/Edge-TTS IDs aren't interchangeable |
| 10 | Durable Job Store, single SSE hub with resume, `GET /jobs/:id` | Slow expensive jobs must survive refresh/restart |
| 11 | Explicit content-addressed Asset Store; `assetId` over URL | Blobs need a home; immutability underpins continuity |
| 12 | Separate Creator Kit (static, versioned) from Project Bundle (per episode) | Kit stays testable; projects stay portable |
| 13 | `@studio/contracts` shared schemas | One definition for three consumers |

